ried slightly across these visits, with the highest blood pressure recorded at 152/83 and the lowest at 139/93. His weight fluctuated between 166 and 181 pounds.\n\nVital Signs:\nThroughout his recorded visits, Mr. Fisher's blood pressure and weight were monitored and recorded. The highest blood pressure was 152/83, and the lowest was 139/93. His weight ranged from 166 pounds to 181 pounds, with the most recent weight being 177 pounds.\n\nFamily History:\nMr. Fisher's family history includes a notable case of colon cancer in his mother, who was diagnosed at the age of 48 and passed away at"
